@page "/signal-complex-domain"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Signal Complex Domain</PageTitle>

<h1>Signal Complex Domain</h1>

<p>Trace of the <em>signal-complex-domain</em> example from <code>HtmlFlow-Datastar-Examples</code>.
    In BRHC, nested signals (<code>data-signals={person:{name,age}}</code>, <code>$person.name</code>)
    express a composite domain and the buttons issue <code>@@put</code> to mutate server state.
    Here the nested object is a C# <code>record</code> - static typing replaces the signal
    path. <strong>Teaching note:</strong> the UHF seeks to give this nested object a static type
    on the server; in Blazor that already exists out of the box, but <em>it is not hypermedia</em> - there
    are no declarative attributes in the HTML; everything is imperative code in the component.</p>

    <div class="demo-box">
        <dl class="row">
            <dt class="col-sm-3">Name</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9">@person.Name</dd>
            <dt class="col-sm-3">Age</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9">@person.Age</dd>
        </dl>

        <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="IncreaseAge">Increase Age</button>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="SwitchUser">Switch User</button>
    </div>

@code {
    // Nested object equivalent to BRHC's {person:{name,age}} signal.
    private sealed record Person(string Name, int Age);

    private Person person = new("John", 30);

    private static readonly Person[] Users =
    [
        new("John", 30),
        new("Jane", 25),
    ];

    private int userIndex;

    // Equivale ao @@put('/signal-complex-domain/increase-age').
    private void IncreaseAge() => person = person with { Age = person.Age + 1 };

    // Equivale ao @put('/signal-complex-domain/switch-user').
    private void SwitchUser()
    {
        userIndex = (userIndex + 1) % Users.Length;
        person = Users[userIndex];
    }
}